    "answer": {
      "short": "Divide by $10\\,000$: area involves two dimensions, so the conversion factor is $100^2$, not $100$.",
      "worked": "The student used the length conversion factor. Each dimension scales by $100$, so the area scales by $100^2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}1\\text{ m}^2&=100\\text{ cm}\\times100\\text{ cm}\\\\1\\text{ m}^2&=10\\,000\\text{ cm}^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nTo convert $\\text{cm}^2$ to $\\text{m}^2$, divide by $10\\,000$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
